+# Primary methods sources and reading limits
+
+Targeted methods consultation, not an exhaustive methodology review. Source identifiers are local to this prepass, not replacements for #1 registry IDs. All accesses were on 2026-10-04. Source text/figures are not redistributed. Web-hosted software documentation is unpinned; production analysis must pin package versions and archive the chosen method specification.
+
+## M01 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 6: Choosing effect measures and computing estimates of effect
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-06
+
+Locator: 6.1.2.2; 6.2.1–6.2.9; 6.3; 6.4.1. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Effect of interest versus scale; participant/trial units; paired/clustered data; extraction of suitable contrast uncertainty.
+
+## M02 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 23: Including variants on randomized trials
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-23
+
+Locator: 23.2.3–23.2.4; 23.2.7–23.2.7.4; 23.3.4–23.3.5. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Paired effects and correlation sensitivity; carryover/period issues; shared-control options.
+
+## M03 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 9: Preparing for synthesis
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-09
+
+Locator: 9.1; 9.3.2–9.3.4, especially 9.3.3 and Table 9.3.c. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Synthesis-specific questions; prespecified selection or aggregation of interchangeable measurements; document grouping changes.
+
+## M04 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 10: Analysing data and undertaking meta-analyses
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-10
+
+Locator: 10.3; 10.10.3–10.10.4, particularly 10.10.4.3–10.10.4.5. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Random effects does not cure incompatible questions; uncertainty and prediction limitations with few studies; REML/HKSJ considerations.
+
+## M05 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 12: Other synthesis methods
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-12
+
+Locator: 12.2.1–12.2.2.1; chapter key points. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Structured non-pooled synthesis; summary distributions without falsely precise pooled means; reject significance vote counting.
+
+## M06 — Cochrane Handbook v6.5 (2024), Chapter 5: Collecting data
+
+Source: https://training.cochrane.org/handbook/current/chapter-05
+
+Locator: 5.2.1: Studies (not reports) as the unit of interest. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Link multiple reports; preserve secondary details without counting the same study twice.
+
+## M07 — Lakens (2013), Calculating and reporting effect sizes to facilitate cumulative science
+
+Source: https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychology/articles/10.3389/fpsyg.2013.00863/full
+
+Locator: Sections on standardized mean differences in within-subjects designs; Table 1; DOI 10.3389/fpsyg.2013.00863. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Specify the denominator: d_z, d_av and between-groups d/g are not interchangeable. Small-sample correction does not erase that distinction.
+
+## M08 — ICH E9(R1) addendum (2019), estimands and sensitivity analysis
+
+Source: https://database.ich.org/sites/default/files/E9-R1_Step4_Guideline_2019_1203.pdf
+
+Locator: A.3.2 principal-stratum paragraph; A.3.3–A.3.4; printed pp.9–10, zero-based PDF pages10–11. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Treatment, population, variable, event strategy and population summary define the question. Adapting this clinical planning framework to HCI is our proposal, not an ICH compliance claim.
+
+## M09 — Campbell et al. (2020), SWiM checklist accompanying Synthesis without meta-analysis in systematic reviews
+
+Source: https://www.equator-network.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/Synthesis-without-Meta-analysis-SWiM-Checklist.pdf
+
+Locator: Checklist pp.1–2, items1–9; both page images inspected; parent article DOI 10.1136/bmj.l6890. Reading: `full_item_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+The two-page checklist was read, not the complete BMJ explanation article. Map grouping, metric, method, prioritization, heterogeneity, certainty, presentation, results and limits.
+
+## M10 — NASA, NASA Task Load Index (TLX), official instrument overview
+
+Source: https://www.nasa.gov/human-systems-integration-division/nasa-task-load-index-tlx/
+
+Locator: Heading NASA Task Load Index (TLX), first two paragraphs and six subscale list; page marked historical reference. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Subjective multidimensional workload; weighted overall score and six subscales. This overview does not establish interchangeability of raw/weighted scores or other workload instruments.
+
+## M11 — Heitz (2014), The speed-accuracy tradeoff: history, physiology, methodology, and behavior
+
+Source: https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/neuroscience/articles/10.3389/fnins.2014.00150/full
+
+Locator: SAT methodology: experimental manipulations and analysis techniques, opening paragraph; SAT manipulations / Verbal instructions; DOI 10.3389/fnins.2014.00150. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+A single speed/accuracy operating point mixes task demands and decision strategy. Preserve both outcomes and task instructions.
+
+## M12 — metafor, Some Recommended Practices, official package documentation
+
+Source: https://wviechtb.github.io/metafor/reference/misc-recs.html
+
+Locator: Dependent estimates workflow: construct V, rma.mv, robust with clubSandwich; footnote on low degrees of freedom. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+Sampling covariance and true-effect heterogeneity are separate modelling layers; robust inference follows a stated working model.
+
+## M13 — clubSandwich, Meta-analysis with cluster-robust variance estimation, official author documentation
+
+Source: https://jepusto.github.io/clubSandwich/articles/meta-analysis-with-CRVE.html
+
+Locator: Multilevel meta-analysis example, coef_test with CR2; coefficient-specific Satterthwaite df and explicit cluster note. Reading: `selected_ranges_read`; access: `full_text_available`.
+
+CR2 and coefficient-specific degrees of freedom; explicitly choose the independent cluster. This software was inspected, not installed or executed here.
+
+## M14 — Pustejovsky and Tipton (2022), Meta-analysis with Robust Variance Estimation: Expanding the Range of Working Models
+
+Source: https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s11121-021-01246-3
+
+Locator: Publisher abstract only; Prevention Science 23,425–438; online 2021; DOI 10.1007/s11121-021-01246-3. Reading: `abstract_only_read`; access: `abstract_only`.
+
+Background lead only. Full paper not read; detailed operational recommendations in this packet rely on M12/M13, not an inferred full-paper reading.
+
+## Prior methodology findings
+
+Retrieved prior-chat orientation describes 1A/1B/1C1 work on RQ-to-method mapping, record families, reporting-versus-conduct distinctions and CIS adaptation, while deferring statistical/non-pooling rules. Their original packets are not mounted in this task workspace and were not re-opened or hash-verified. These summaries therefore informed scope only, not source claims or numerical assumptions. Current assessed repository authorities independently require the unresolved quantitative decisions. The auditory-review access investigation was not repeated.
+
+## M15 — Röver, Knapp and Friede (2015)
+
+Source: https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12874-015-0091-1
+
+Locator: Methods / Parameter estimation and Confidence intervals and tests, equations(5)–(11); Conclusions paragraphs1–3. Full text available; selected ranges read. The inspected equations define inverse-total-variance weighting, q, and q*=max(1,q). The modification can be conservative with few studies; it is not a universal guarantee. The article, not its arXiv version, is the basis used here.
